sub:Head {
  this: a np:Nanopublication ;
    np:hasAssertion sub:assertion ;
    np:hasProvenance sub:provenance ;
    np:hasPublicationInfo sub:pubinfo .
}

sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-ch02-06> dct:description "Proof scope of the kernel-checked statement recorded as thompson1917-ch02-06: 4 statement(s) the Lean kernel checked and 3 assumption(s) stated in the module header and not proved. The source's claim (\"Power needed for flight grows as length^3.5 while muscle power grows as length^3\", On Growth and Form 1917) is what the statement was written FROM, not what was checked." ;
    skos:scopeNote "Kernel-checked: Exact: lift = ½ ρ v² S C_L equal to weight with 0 < C_L ≤ C_L,max implies v ≥ sqrt(2W/(ρ S C_L,max)) (vmin_le)." ;
    skos:scopeNote "Kernel-checked: Under R1, R2, constant ρ and C_L,max: v_min(L2)/v_min(L1) = sqrt(L2/L1), log exponent 1/2 (vmin_ratio, vmin_log)." ;
    skos:scopeNote "Kernel-checked: With constant L/D, power required at v_min: ratio (L2/L1)^3 sqrt(L2/L1), log exponent 7/2 (powerRequired_ratio, powerRequired_log)." ;
    skos:scopeNote "Kernel-checked: Under MusclePowerLaw (named hypothesis) and R1: power available ratio (L2/L1)^3 (powerAvailable_ratio); P_req/P_avail = c sqrt(L) with an explicit c (powerRatio_eq)." ;
    skos:scopeNote "Assumed, not proved: Constant C_L,max across sizes (Reynolds effects change it), constant ρ, constant L/D, and flight at v_min rather than a faster, more efficient speed." ;
    skos:scopeNote "Assumed, not proved: The muscle premise of Thompson (muscle fraction f and mass-specific power p constant) is contested: contraction frequency falls with size, so the modern expectation is an exponent below 3. It is carried as a hypothesis, never proved or asserted." ;
    skos:scopeNote "Assumed, not proved: The physics thread found one Cypselurus hiraii specimen inside its v_min envelope (v_min 9.85 m/s against field speeds 10-20 m/s) but could not test the sqrt(W/S) scaling with its data; the theorems are statements about the model, not confirmed facts." ;
    rdfs:comment "The kernel-checked statements are theorems of the model; the assumptions are the model. Does not establish: anything about organisms. The theorem is exact inside the stated model and silent outside it. The assumptions it rests on, written in the module header and never proved, are: Constant C_L,max across sizes (Reynolds effects change it), constant ρ, constant L/D, and flight at v_min rather than a faster, more efficient speed; The muscle premise of Thompson (muscle fraction f and mass-specific power p constant) is contested: contraction frequency falls with size, so the modern expectation is an exponent below 3. It is carried as a hypothesis, never proved or asserted; The physics thread found one Cypselurus hiraii specimen inside its v_min envelope (v_min 9.85 m/s against field speeds 10-20 m/s) but could not test the sqrt(W/S) scaling with its data; the theorems are statements about the model, not confirmed facts. Kernel-checked is not expert-validated: no human expert has validated these statements. Whether the Lean statement faithfully renders the source is a separate assessment record, and so far only one assessor provider has run." ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/4ebb56add61de66744fe8b957ecd7c0bcecc8083/lean/Delphi/Scaling.lean> .
}

sub:provenance {
  sub:assertion prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-lean-thread-builder> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/4ebb56add61de66744fe8b957ecd7c0bcecc8083/lean/Delphi/Scaling.lean> , <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/lean/lean.json> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-lean-thread-builder> a prov:SoftwareAgent ;
    rdfs:label "delphisci lean thread (Claude Fable 5.1 writing the Lean modules and this builder; the Lean kernel, not the model, checked the proofs)" ;
    delphi:usesModel <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a delphi:LanguageModel ;
    rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1" ;
    dct:identifier "claude-fable-5-1" .
}

